hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27629","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bishr, he said: Haddathana Hani' ibn Uthman al-Juhani, from his mother Humaydah bint Yasir, from her grandmother Yusayrah, and she was among the emigrant women, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: O believing women, upon you be tahlil and tasbih and taqdis, and do not be heedless lest you forget mercy, and count with the fingertips, for they will be questioned and made to speak."
